sitting at my typewriter.

485
00:25:09,800 --> 00:25:10,951
I had written all night.

486
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:12,631
He rewrote the whole fucking script.

487
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:16,100
- Billy, I love it.

488
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:18,100
It's perfect.

489
00:25:18,253 --> 00:25:20,400
Hey boys, I'm excited to get into this.

490
00:25:21,100 --> 00:25:22,300
Did we pay this guy yet?

491
00:25:24,733 --> 00:25:26,669
- Billy walsh, our director.
- Steve.

492
00:25:30,700 --> 00:25:33,367
$275,000 down the drain.

493
00:25:33,527 --> 00:25:35,148
But I have to admit, the script is good.

494
00:25:35,257 --> 00:25:37,328
- No, it's great.
- It is great.

495
00:25:37,507 --> 00:25:40,499
And Gaghan was kind enough to read it
and agree before he headed back home.

496
00:25:40,500 --> 00:25:42,100
- Thank you so much.
- Hey, no problem.

497
00:25:42,200 --> 00:25:44,100
I've had people read
my work and not like it,

498
00:25:44,200 --> 00:25:46,900
but I've never
had anybody pay me not to work.

499
00:25:47,900 --> 00:25:49,197
It was nice, actually.

500
00:25:50,014 --> 00:25:52,029
FINAL DAY OF PRODUCTION (del vo)

501
00:25:52,277 --> 00:25:53,605
All right, this is our last shot.

502
00:25:53,650 --> 00:25:55,800
Probably the most complicated
of the whole shoot.

503
00:25:55,912 --> 00:25:57,392
And I'm not in it, which is nice.

504
00:25:57,500 --> 00:25:59,832
Which is why we're both
a little toasty right now.

505
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:02,700
- What?
- You're gonna have to edit that out.

506
00:26:03,591 --> 00:26:05,257
So Eric, what's this scene?

507
00:26:05,700 --> 00:26:08,920
Okay, the army storms Pablo's hideout.

508
00:26:09,400 --> 00:26:11,837
Explosions go off
in the south, east and west.

509
00:26:12,100 --> 00:26:14,314
We have nine cameras
pointed at everything Billy wants.

510
00:26:14,395 --> 00:26:16,737
We've been prepping
this for three months. It has to work.

511
00:26:16,915 --> 00:26:19,392
- We can't do it twice.
- Okay, are you ready for this?

512
00:26:20,300 --> 00:26:22,139
Are we fucking ready?!

513
00:26:23,822 --> 00:26:25,196
Nobody sounds fucking ready.

514
00:26:25,300 --> 00:26:28,000
Hey, get that fucking camera off me.
I'll throw it in the water.

515
00:26:28,288 --> 00:26:29,324
He's nervous.

516
00:26:29,500 --> 00:26:30,926
Looks like he has it under control.

517
00:26:32,300 --> 00:26:33,347
You freaking?

518
00:26:34,500 --> 00:26:35,691
A little bit.

519
00:26:36,430 --> 00:26:39,300
- It's all good, Billy.
- Everything is prepared.

520
00:26:39,500 --> 00:26:42,100
If we get this shot, guys,
we got the whole movie in the can.

521
00:26:42,800 --> 00:26:44,241
Let's do it.
Let's do it.

522
00:26:44,400 --> 00:26:45,641
Let's do it!

523
00:26:47,600 --> 00:26:48,797
Roll cameras!

524
00:26:50,900 --> 00:26:52,300
Set!
We're ready.

525
00:27:22,349 --> 00:27:24,848
Let's kill this motherfucker! (del vo)

526
00:27:49,800 --> 00:27:50,800
Cut!

527
00:27:53,500 --> 00:27:55,750
The start was off, suit.
I'm gonna need another one.

528
00:27:57,300 --> 00:27:59,401
I'm fucking with you.
It was perfect!

529
00:28:05,650 --> 00:28:07,767
- Guys, we did it.
- Yes, we did.

530
00:28:07,877 --> 00:28:10,151
Who would have thought
some kids from Queens could have?

531
00:28:10,152 --> 00:28:12,057
But we did,
and it's gonna be fucking amazing.

532
00:28:12,115 --> 00:28:15,000
I've never felt so good about a movie
after it was done than this one.

533
00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:17,019
I know it.

534
00:28:19,571 --> 00:28:20,900
You think you made a good film?

535
00:28:21,800 --> 00:28:22,800
I'll tell you this:

536
00:28:23,300 --> 00:28:25,795
it's either going to be genius or it's
going to fucking suck.

537
00:28:26,203 --> 00:28:28,100
Until I see the first cut,
I have no idea.

538
00:28:28,253 --> 00:28:31,300
But you know what?
Neither does anybody else.

